From 97f4900e057c84f146edfdabe35ff8d59c314809 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:59:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(post): Heidenhain DIN/ISO stops for a manual tool
 change

On a machine that states tooling.tool_change = "manual-retract-top"
(the Fehlmann Picomax 55, iTNC 530), the DIN/ISO post now writes, at
each tool change: G00 G90 Z+0 M92 under the old tool call, the
operator checks, M6 (MP 7440 bit 0 = 0 halts there), then the new T
block. The first tool gets the checks and M6 only.

New engine law: a script on a manual tool change machine must declare
the mode in manualToolChange, or the engine refuses the pair by name
(post and machine) before any hook runs. heidenhain.cps and
heidenhain-klartext.cps declare manual-retract-top.

Fixes #4085

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
